# m-control rules (Cursor)

Canonical context lives in the repo docs — read these before changing code:

1. `docs/ai/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` — product context
2. `docs/architecture/constraints.md` — hard rules (the constitution)
3. `docs/architecture/execution-model.md` — Tool Protocol v1 spec
4. `docs/ai/CODING-GUIDELINES.md` — patterns and naming
5. `CLAUDE.md` — condensed working rules (shared source of truth)

## Layout (monorepo, Yarn workspaces)

- `packages/core` — runtime engine `@m-control/core`, library only; public API is `src/index.ts`
- `apps/mctl` — CLI binary, imports `@m-control/core` (never internal paths)
- `tools/<category>/<id>/` — standalone tool processes, NOT npm packages, any language
- `templates/node-tool`, `templates/python-tool` — boilerplate for new tools

## Build order

`yarn build` from the repo root (core first, then mctl). Never run
`yarn install` inside a package directory.

## Tool Protocol v1 (never violate)

- Tool stdout = NDJSON ToolEvent lines ONLY; no raw prints
- Tool stdin = single JSON ToolRequest, read to EOF before executing
- Event sequence: `started` → `log`* → `result` | `error`; exit 0/1/≥2
- Every tool dir has `manifest.json` with `manifestVersion: 1`, `id`, `runtime`, `entry`

## Never

- `console.log` in `packages/` or `apps/` production code (use EventSink)
- Throw raw `Error` — use the hierarchy from `@m-control/core` (see `.claude/rules/errors.md`)
- Hardcode paths — use `path.resolve()` or config
- Change `packages/core` public API without updating `src/index.ts`
